<title>USA: TABLE-Equity Corp Q2 net income increases.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Equity Corp Q2 net income increases.</headline>
<dateline>LUFKIN, Texas 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Equity Corporation International</p>
<p>	   For the Three Months Ended  For the Six Months Ended</p>
<p>		 6/30/97     6/30/96	 6/30/97     6/30/96</p>
<p>Revenues: $30,912,000   21,526,000    63,166,000   44,606,000</p>
<p>Total gross profit</p>
<p>	    $8,335,000    6,134,000    18,335,000   13,520,000</p>
<p>Operating income</p>
<p>	    $6,236,000    4,839,000    14,501,000   10,640,000</p>
<p>Net income</p>
<p>	    $3,056,000   $2,645,000    $7,546,000   $4,882,000</p>
<p>Earnings per share</p>
<p>	    $.15	   $.14(b)	 $.36	   $.29(b)</p>
<p>Weighted average number of shares outstanding</p>
<p>	  21,028,000   18,273,000(b) 20,721,000   16,679,000(b)</p>
<p>NOTE: -- (a) Reflects a charge for the required change in the company's Federal Income Tax rate from 34 percent to 35 percent of $565,000, to revalue deferred tax liabilities.</p>
<p>-- (b) Restated to reflect the company's 3-for-2 stock split effective October 2, 1996.</p>
<p>((--New York Newsdesk 212-859-1700))</p>
</text>
